<%= render "shared/errors", record: program %>
<%= form_with model: program.persisted? ? program : [program.venue, program] do |form| %>
  <p><%= form.label :name %><br><%= form.text_field :name, required: true, maxlength: 100 %></p>
  <p><%= form.label :program_label, "Program label" %><br><%= form.text_field :program_label, required: true, maxlength: 40 %><br><small>Singular label, such as Program or Workshop.</small></p>
  <p><%= form.label :participant_label, "Participant label" %><br><%= form.text_field :participant_label, required: true, maxlength: 40 %><br><small>Singular label for the person booked, such as Participant or Instructor. This changes terminology, not booking rules.</small></p>
  <p><%= form.label :custom_slug, "Slug" %><br><%= form.text_field :custom_slug, maxlength: 100, placeholder: program.name.to_s.to_url %><br>
    <small>Leave blank to generate from the <%= @program.program_label.downcase %> name. Previous links keep working when the slug changes. <% if program.persisted? %>Current link: <%= link_to program_url(program), program_path(program) %>.<% end %></small>
  </p>
  <p>Venue: <%= link_to program.venue.name, venue_path(program.venue) %></p>
  <p><%= form.label :time_zone, "Time zone" %><br><%= form.select :time_zone, Program::TIME_ZONES, {}, required: true %></p>
  <p><%= form.label :start_time, "Regular start time" %><br><%= form.time_field :start_time, required: true, step: 60 %><br>
    <small>Usual event start in the <%= @program.program_label.downcase %>'s time zone. Use Manage Schedule to change a single date.</small>
  </p>
  <p><%= form.label :end_time, "Regular end time (optional)" %><br><%= form.time_field :end_time, step: 60 %><br>
    <small>An earlier end time means the next day. Leave blank if the end time is not known.</small>
  </p>
  <p><%= form.label :calendar_invitation_lead_minutes, "Calendar invitation lead time (minutes)" %><br>
    <%= form.number_field :calendar_invitation_lead_minutes, min: 0, step: 1, required: true %><br>
    <small>Google Calendar invitations start this many minutes before the booked <%= program.program_label.downcase %>. Defaults to 0. Booking times and calendar end times stay unchanged. Changing this also updates existing upcoming invitations.</small>
  </p>
  <p><%= form.label :pay, "Pay (USD)" %><br><%= form.number_field :pay, min: 0, step: "0.01", required: true %></p>
  <p><%= form.label :booking_horizon_months, "Booking horizon (months)" %><br><%= form.number_field :booking_horizon_months, min: 1, required: true %></p>
  <fieldset>
    <legend>Available Weekdays</legend>
    <%= hidden_field_tag "program[available_weekdays][]", "" %>
    <% Date::DAYNAMES.each_with_index do |day, index| %>
      <label><%= check_box_tag "program[available_weekdays][]", index, program.available_weekdays.include?(index.to_s), id: "weekday-#{index}" %> <%= day %></label>
    <% end %>
  </fieldset>
  <fieldset>
    <legend>Prevent Consecutive <%= @program.participant_label.pluralize.titleize %> by Gender</legend>
    <p>Optional. When enabled, each selected gender cannot repeat in immediately adjacent scheduled <%= @program.program_label.pluralize.downcase %>. Unselected genders may repeat. An unbooked <%= @program.program_label.downcase %> breaks the sequence; closed dates are skipped.</p>
    <%= hidden_field_tag "program[no_consecutive_genders][]", "" %>
    <% User::GENDERS.each do |gender| %>
      <label><%= check_box_tag "program[no_consecutive_genders][]", gender, program.no_consecutive_genders.include?(gender), id: "no-consecutive-#{gender}" %> <%= gender.capitalize %></label>
    <% end %>
    <p>These rules apply to new bookings and replacements, not existing reservations. Organizers can explicitly override with an explanation.</p>
  </fieldset>
  <p><%= form.label :instructions %><br><%= form.text_area :instructions, maxlength: 5000, rows: 4 %></p>
  <p>Changing regular times updates upcoming bookings without a dated time exception, retaining each time change. Other settings do not rewrite existing bookings. Automated reminders are not available yet.</p>
  <%= form.submit program.persisted? ? "Save #{@program.program_label.titleize}" : "Create #{@program.program_label.titleize}" %>
<% end %>
